 tied to qualifying starter home construction\" and \"Expand incentives for building and selling ADUs as entry-level homes\". Those meet the subsidy clauses of rung 4. Rung 4's other clause, \"Set no binding rules\", is never stated anywhere in the sources. A freeze on *new* regulations and complaints about \"mandates\" don't reject rent caps or required affordable units, and the codebook says silence is not a clause. The starter-home page is also undated, and undated statements can't seat a chair.\n\n**How the passages were coded:**\n- **Interview and debates (2026-04-12, 05-07, 05-15):** own words answering the housing question. All of them only show a lean toward deregulation (`direction-only`).\n- **Fee-cap, VMT and new-cities pages:** written in the third person (\"Steve Hilton will…\"), so they count as someone describing him, not his own words. The new-cities plan is about where to build, so it's `adjacent` to this question.\n- **College page, CalMatters excerpt and the empty page:** off-topic or not evidence.\n\n**What's missing (listed in `needs_source`):**\n- Hilton's own words on rent caps or rent control.\n- His own words on inclusionary zoning or required affordable units.\n- A dated copy of the starter-home page.\n\nThe file also tiers four quotes from his own words: two as `lever` and two as `direction`.\n\nSix claude.ai connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey, WorkOS) need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and the GitHub plugin failed to connect. None of them was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":21515,"type":"result","duration_ms":56906,"uuid":"1751ef0d-e794-44aa-9f5e-44f9a07626db","ttft_stream_ms":1585,"time_to_request_ms":87,"first_content_frame_ms":1585,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
